  <prompt>Create the unified `RecordCreationService` in `Services/RecordCreation/` by porting the create half of `OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` (~:302 of `Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs`) behind the 12-step FR-06 pipeline, with a caller principal (WhoAmI, 403 when unresolved) and a system principal. Failures are typed refusals `(Kind, Code, Detail)` mapped to ProblemDetails by ONE shared map. Field mapping (step 3) is only a no-op seam in this task; task 014 wires it. Re-point DI so the unified service replaces the Office registration at `OfficeModule.cs:73` without breaking compile.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse write-path security. Follow ADRs strictly; this code decides who may create what.</role>
  <goal>`RecordCreationService` (sealed, scoped, registered once) runs the 12 FR-06 steps in order for the caller and system principals, makes exactly one app-only create call, returns typed refusals, and a single shared map renders them as ProblemDetails with a stable `errorCode`. A seam test asserts step order and one create call for a root (Matter) and a child (Event).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-06, FR-07, FR-12 and the "New Components" table; design.md §4. Two cores exist today: `OwnedChildWrite` (create half, children, strong authorization) and the Office `RecordCreationService` (roots, weaker authorization). Task 011 extracted the caller checks into `CallerWriteAuthorization`; task 012 produced `RecordTableRules`. This task composes them. Steps (spec FR-06): 1 resolve principal; 2 table rules, refuse blocked columns in the caller payload; 3 field mapping (NO-OP seam here); 4 map merged payload; 5 caller checks on merged payload (via CallerWriteAuthorization); 6 secure-root plan; 7 owner (ResolveOwnerAsync in task 015 - here keep the ported owner behaviour behind one method so 015 swaps it); 8 search-index default (task 015, seam); 9 creator person, "for" person, table defaults; 10 I-1 stamp + I-16 derived; 11 one app-only create with alternate-key retry for autonumber tables; 12 post-create steps (number read-back, isolated-root completion, sharee mirror, assigned-access grants, membership event), never throwing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationRefusal.cs (Kind, Code, Detail; typed refusal record)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationProblemMap.cs (the ONE refusal-kind to ProblemDetails map)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Office/RecordCreationServicePipelineSeamTests.cs (grep tests/integration/seam/README.md for the seam folder rule; place under the folder it prescribes)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (CreateAsync ~:302 is the porting source; stays compiling until 017 removes the create half)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs (rename class to OfficeRecordCreationService or namespace-qualify; deleted by task 018)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs (field `_recordCreation` ~:77 and ctor ~:107 follow the rename)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/OfficeModule.cs (registration ~:73)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs (task 011 output)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (task 012 output)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (ResolveOwnerAsync ~:1016, ForParents ~:346)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="required">CallerWriteAuthorization exists and is behaviour-identical to the old OwnedChildWrite helpers.</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="required">RecordTableRules registry exists; an arch test requires an entry per create table.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: payload-dependent authorization. Checks that depend on the request body (every lookup, the regarding pair, mapped values) live in `CallerWriteAuthorization` and are CALLED by the service; they are NOT written as endpoint filters. Route-level authorization (RequireAuthorization, caller identity, route ledger) stays in filters. Cite path A in the PR description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: refusals. Every refusal Kind maps to ProblemDetails with a stable `errorCode` and a correlation id; no raw upstream/Dataverse exception text in the response; detail goes to logs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. The create is app-only under the managed identity; the caller identity is resolved by WhoAmI on the CALLER's token (reuse CallerWriteAuthorization's WhoAmI). Unresolved WhoAmI returns 403 and writes nothing. System principal skips as-caller checks (steps 2 and 5) only and records `RequestedBy` when known.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. One scoped registration of `RecordCreationService` replaces the single registration at OfficeModule.cs ~:73; no interface unless a second implementation is needed (the engine stays static). No new background service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: every caller check. Fail closed: an exception, timeout or unresolved lookup in any caller check REFUSES the create (uniform 404 for "does not exist" and "cannot see"); it never falls through to a create. Mapping must never become an existence oracle.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: behaviour. This task ports behaviour; do not change the owner rule (task 015), wire mapping (task 014) or touch Repair mode (016). Step 3 is a documented no-op seam; steps 7-8 call the ported owner logic through ONE private method each so 015 can swap them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: name clash. The Office class is also named `RecordCreationService`. Rename it `OfficeRecordCreationService` (preferred) or namespace-qualify at every use; record the choice in the task notes. Task 018 deletes it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. State a Placement Justification in the PR (BFF; synchronous write path, spec "Placement" section); measure publish-size delta against a fresh master build per root CLAUDE.md §10.4; run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; add no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added by this task. Seam test under tests/integration/seam/**; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

