  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-06/07/12, design §4, the exemplar's neighbours 011/012 outputs; re-grep `OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` callers, `RecordCreationService` usages and `OfficeModule.cs` registration.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check (UAC-r2 PR #2110 also edits OwnedChildWrite.cs, ChildRecordEndpoints.cs and CommunicationService.cs); record the result in the task notes. Stop and escalate if a PR rewrites OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the typed refusal (Kind, Code, Detail) with a closed Kind set (for example: BlockedColumn, NotFoundOrDenied, Forbidden, PrincipalUnresolved, OwnerUnresolved, Invalid, Conflict, Upstream) and the single shared `RecordCreationProblemMap` to ProblemDetails + stable `errorCode`. Include a unit test that every Kind has a mapping (reflection over the enum).</step>
    <step order="3">Rename the Office class (see constraint) and fix its references; build.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `RecordCreationService.CreateAsync(RecordCreationRequest, RecordCreationPrincipal, ct)` returning a result that is either the created id + warnings or a refusal. Port from OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync, reading rules from RecordTableRules and calling CallerWriteAuthorization for steps 2 and 5. Implement caller principal (WhoAmI under caller token, 403 when unresolved) and system principal (skip steps 2 and 5, record RequestedBy).</step>
    <step order="5">Post-create step 12 must catch and log, never throw; the create result still returns. Use the existing alternate-key retry for autonumber tables (do not retry blindly after an ambiguous failure, NFR-03).</step>
    <step order="6">Replace the OfficeModule.cs registration so the unified service is registered once (scoped) and the renamed Office class stays registered until 018.</step>
    <step order="7">Write the seam test: a recording fake for each step asserts the step ORDER and that exactly ONE create call is made, for a Matter (root) and an Event (child); plus caller-principal-unresolved returns 403 with no create; plus system principal skips steps 2 and 5 but runs every other step.</step>
    <step order="8">Build, run SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests and the Office quick-create contract tests unchanged; measure publish size; run the CVE check.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the 12 FR-06 steps cannot be ordered as written without changing existing OwnedChildWrite behaviour (for example the secure-root plan needs the owner before step 6), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the two orderings.</trigger>
    <trigger>If /conflict-check shows UAC-r2 PR #2110 changes OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync, STOP and ask the human to sequence the work.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any caller-check path cannot be made to fail closed (it swallows an exception today), escalate as a security finding before porting it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `class RecordCreationService` and `static .* CreateAsync` in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api: Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs (roots, 1264 lines) and Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs ~:302 (children); callers: ChildRecordEndpoints.cs ~:258, DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs ~:341, EmailDraftToolHandler.cs ~:455, BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs ~:242.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, by merging the two existing cores into one; net one service replaces two creation cores, per the spec section 11 table ("Yes: merges the two existing cores"). A separate refusal type and map file are small value types that the three callers (route, Office, chat) share.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The same Project filed under the same Matter gets different owners by surface, mapping reaches 2 of about 30 create paths, and chat creates skip the I-1 stamp and I-16 (spec section 11 table).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

