  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`RecordCreationService` is `sealed`, registered exactly once as scoped, and the Office class is renamed (or qualified) with the choice recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A seam test asserts the 12-step order and exactly one create call for a Matter (root) and an Event (child); mapping step 3 is a recorded no-op.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Caller principal: WhoAmI is resolved under the caller token; an unresolved WhoAmI returns a refusal that maps to HTTP 403 and issues zero create calls.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">System principal: steps 2 and 5 are skipped, RequestedBy is recorded when supplied, and every other step runs; a test shows a system create and a caller create under the same parent get the same stamp and owner path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One shared map turns every refusal Kind into ProblemDetails with a stable `errorCode` and correlation id; a test fails if a Kind has no mapping; no response body contains raw upstream exception text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller-check exception or an unresolved lookup refuses the create (no create call is issued) and a payload naming a blocked column is refused before any Dataverse write; "does not exist" and "cannot see" return the identical status and body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 12 post-create failures are logged and do not throw: the create result is still returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests and the Office quick-create contract tests pass unchanged; publish-size delta, CVE result and the /conflict-check result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From UAC-r2's 011 review (K2, 2026-10-20): the OwnedChildWrite / CallerWriteAuthorization mutual `using static` cannot silently rebind. Either qualify every cross-class call (and drop the using-static) or add an ArchTest asserting the two types share no member names, with must-fire and must-not-fire controls.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

